  "Question": "In triangle \\(ABC\\), \\(|\\sin A-1/2|+(\\tan B-1)^2=0\\), and both \\(\\angle A\\) and \\(\\angle B\\) are acute angles. Find the measure of \\(\\angle C\\) in degrees.",
  "Choices": {},
  "Correct Answer": "105",
  "Accepted Answers": [],
  "Unordered Answers": false,
  "Solution": "If the sum of two nonnegative numbers is 0, both must be 0. Thus, \\(\\sin A=1/2\\) gives \\(\\angle A=30^\\circ\\), and \\(\\tan B=1\\) gives \\(\\angle B=45^\\circ\\). Therefore, \\(\\angle C=180^\\circ-30^\\circ-45^\\circ=105^\\circ\\).",
